  ]},
  { cards: [zoroOp13], title: "OP13-037 Roronoa Zoro — Alternative 7-DON!! Option", paragraphs: [
    "This version of Zoro sets 2 DON!! Active on play and also sets itself Active at the end of your turn.",
    "It is an alternative to OP16-035 Roronoa Zoro for players who want a less expensive option while keeping DON!! immediately available for their Leader."
  ]},
  { cards: [chopperNine], title: "OP18-029 Tony Tony.Chopper", paragraphs: [
    "This 9-cost, 6000-Power Character has Rush and +1000 Counter.",
    "When it attacks, once per turn, its effect attaches 3 rested DON!! to your Leader and sets Chopper Active. In exchange, Chopper cannot become Active during your next Refresh Phase.",
    "Keeping Chopper Active after its first attack on the turn you play it can prepare a particularly aggressive turn.",
    "If it is still available on your next turn, the combination with Gonbe and Chimney can let you make up to five attacks: two with Chopper and three with your Leader.",
    "Its main drawback is that it offers less defense than OP18-118 Monkey.D.Luffy. Unlike Luffy, Chopper cannot neutralize an opposing Character, and the 3 DON!! are attached to your Leader rather than set Active, limiting how you can use them.",
    "Monkey.D.Luffy is therefore preferable for maintaining a balance between aggression and defense."
  ]},
  { cards: [namiOp14], title: "OP14-031 Nami", paragraphs: [
    "This version of Nami is an alternative for players who want to focus more on board control.",
    "She can set an opposing Character with a Cost of 8 or less Rested and set 5 DON!! Active at the end of the turn.",
    "This helps you remove opposing Characters while providing additional protection with her Blocker effect."
  ]},
  { cards: [strongEvent], title: "OP13-040 I Know You're Strong... So I'll Go All Out from the Very Start!!!", paragraphs: [
    "This Event is a more defensive alternative to Demon Aura Nine Sword Style Asura Blades Drawn Dead Man's Game.",
    "Counter: give +3000 Power for 1 DON!!.",
    "Main: for a total investment of 3 DON!!, prevent up to two opposing Rested Characters with a Cost of 7 or less from becoming Active during their next Refresh Phase.",
    "It is especially useful for limiting the number of opposing attacks."
  ]},
  { cards: [laboon], title: "OP15-035 Laboon", paragraphs: [
    "Laboon can be considered if the protection from Nico Robin and Sanji is not enough against decks focused on Removal.",
    "Its effect protects your Characters with 7000 Power or less by setting two of your cards Rested. Unlike Sanji, Laboon does not need to be placed in your Trash to use its effect, and Laboon can target itself to pay for its effect.",
    "You can use this protection multiple times as long as you have enough cards to pay its cost.",
    "Its main limitation is that it cannot protect your Characters with more than 7000 Power.",
    "In hand, it is a +2000 Counter."
  ]},
  { cards: [asuraOp07], title: "OP07-036 Demonic Aura Nine-Sword Style Asura Demon Nine Flash", paragraphs: [
    "This 2-cost Event gives +3000 Power and sets an opposing Character with a Cost of 5 or less Rested.",
    "It is another option for setting up lethal, especially by neutralizing an opposing Blocker before your Leader attacks."
  ]}
];

const matchupIntro = [
  "OP18-022 Monkey.D.Luffy is especially effective when he can establish his support Characters and maintain constant pressure through repeated Leader attacks.",
  "The most difficult matchups are those where the opponent can remove Nico Robin, interrupt your attacks with Triggers, or build enough defensive resources to withstand Double Attack."
];
const matchupPositioning = [
  "Green Luffy's main difficulty is its unfavorable matchups against Rocks and Buggy, two Leaders that occupy a significant place in the OP18 meta.",
  "Red Purple Luffy has favorable matchups against both Leaders, while Green Luffy is itself especially favored against Red Purple Luffy.",
